    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_710e636d",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: black friday sale; hasOverallIntent: hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a historical scene of the transatlantic slave trade, with enslaved Africans being brought to a colonial shore by European traders. The juxtaposition of this horrific historical event with the text 'black friday sale' creates a deeply offensive and hateful analogy. It equates the commodification of human beings in slavery with modern consumerism, using the term 'black' to reference both the racial identity of the enslaved people and the color associated with Black Friday sales. This is a form of racialized exploitation and dehumanization, reducing the trauma of slavery to a commercial promotion. The meme is intentionally provocative and harmful, leveraging the historical suffering of Black people to mock or trivialize the Black Friday shopping event, thereby perpetuating anti-Black racism and historical revisionism. The intent is to shock and provoke, but it does so by inflicting pain on a marginalized group through the lens of racialized commerce.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_ed2b5d7e"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
